privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Guix's current registry-native machine comparison needs to inspect a completed LAGOON product's sealed target binding without invoking receiving. This adds `check-target CHANNELS STORE PROFILE TARGET` to the existing Guile driver, reusing the receive/rollback predicate and checking registered, canonical store custody before and after reading.\n\nThe complete [source-owned requirement](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/computer-deployment-engine/blob/1f94535017573c8c6fcb789d7e9d2f3df0372915/content/text/documents/specifications/read-only-target-check.md) defines inputs, observed JSON fields, refusals, trusted-channel prerequisite, preserved target/role semantics and qualification. CHANNELS is previously authenticated trusted Scheme with no effects or stdout output; the existing reader evaluates it. LAGOON's check bypasses profile creation, retention roots, activation and the activation lease. It is neither a sandbox nor source provenance, machine acceptance or deployment permission.\n\nSource custody:\n- Original base: `c40ef8cc715fc61831dd298308198c76f0cd694a`.\n- Previously reviewed head: `abf95bbb0028b1677b8f3611b9736f95c98aa8e4`.\n- Incorporated accepted main: `ddba5d59f9237ca10ce1b2568215b512dda506ae`.\n- Resulting qualified head: `1f94535017573c8c6fcb789d7e9d2f3df0372915`; tree `654dee5d72e6768943a13a53442b05385c21a367`.\n- Reviewed driver `a6de146cb772934df82daeb39d3a5ef0a399c46f`, test `067fd59225046ebd867bbd0e0089e4a5fc5e1772`, specification `35b7168436283d1093180c85ecbf0f8b2b48cfb6` are unchanged. Hosted commit/tree/blob readback completed.\n\nQualification:\n- Complete declared public source suite: 321 Guile/Guix assertions and 25 Node tests passed; exit 0.\n- Exact extracted packed artifact: same complete suite passed, exit 0. Both runs used the sole producer runner and the existing owner supplier closure whose installed/source lock SHA256 is `02368770d0677869e52b24ee135d2dd9fa43a2b2e98c7bd9140c3a774d20a143`. Manifest, lock and configuration hashes stayed unchanged. This is not an independent frozen installation.\n- PNPM pack succeeded: 63,516 bytes, 27 files; SHA256 `7050d598d8def85a618be97aceb6aee016dd9c9c362a993aa2603f16c4fac0db`; integrity `sha512-eLtO41VcH2TvswCDTfuh9ZNK5LbtvZKurShqfaqjdeF5LGDk7f/lU3+f2Co2aurmX+McGarS1MOt0ZwEfFqHqg==`.\n- Strict byte audit returned 1: only package.json differs. Separate reconciliation returned 0: PNPM reordered the scripts key/formatting without changing any parsed manifest value or test command; the other 26 files and modes match exact source.\n- Independent reviewer `/root/independent_contract_review` accepted the final head, read the source/artifact results and independently hashed the archive. The trusted-CHANNELS finding is resolved; no remaining blocking source finding. Reviewer performed no tests or edits.\n\nReady for review; **not qualified for merge yet**. The exact [CD contract, README lines 630–645 at b697963](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/continuous-delivery-services-section/blob/b697963f336ed5c457e2f68e98111ee325213148/README.md#L630-L645) states: “Merge: with a merge commit, by whoever made the change, once the change test reports no-regression.” Executable driver and test-selection changes exclude this PR from both approved source-only exceptions. Local checks/artifact qualification cannot replace that explicit prerequisite. No machine verdict exists for this resulting tree; no protection or gate has been changed.\n\nCurrent failed/unmet native contract and enabling event:\n- [Guix receiver at c54c650](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/blob/c54c65064e678963c00e36edcded771ac473988c/scripts/receive-pull-requests.mjs#L395-L400) returns `outcome: incomplete`, `stage: native-product-receiving`, `runtimeAcceptance: false`, reason: “Native base/candidate fabrication, original engineering obligations and target interfaces have not been received.” This is source readback of the retained v3 route, not a newly executed held request.\n- Enabling event: the Guix owner qualifies the current registry-native paired binding from genuine Code source/consumer/committed-lock/frozen-install/runtime evidence to actual immutable LAGOON products, receives original engineering/target obligations, and records an exact-candidate no-regression verdict. The historical common-root v3 route and this target check cannot be relabeled as that binding.\n- [Guix#101](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/issues/101) / [BCF#765](https://github.com/561-group/bare-cedar-fog/issues/765) remain open. Paired Code evidence/custody was requested from existing BCF writer task `01a14777-efa5-7633-896a-df9e6cdb001d`, under existing `operating-engineering-release-and-recovery` Work; no duplicate install/runner or native allocation was created.\n- Separate native-allocation observation remains unverified: automatic approval review rejected `operations agency` because it was not a clearly supported read-only query and side effects were ambiguous. It was not retried or bypassed. A verified supported read-only interface or explicit authorization for that exact operation enables this observation; it does not waive the machine gate.\n\nNo new version allocated, registry package published, PR merged, machine installed or service activated.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-17T05:54:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T14:44:59Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"red-cup-engineering:read-only-target-check-20261017","ref":"read-only-target-check-20261017","repo":{"id":1420367722,"node_id":"R_kgDOVKkXag","name":"computer-deployment-engine","full_name":"red-cup-engineering/computer-deployment-engine",